# patching-hosts host knob (#658). Grammar: the vendored skill's
# references/knob.md (skills/patching-hosts). The skill reads this file and
# never writes it. Times are UTC. A malformed line makes the host report-only
# until fixed. Check: bash skills/patching-hosts/scripts/read-knob.sh --host "$(hostname)"
# Guard: tests/test_patching_hosts_knob.py.

class production
posture scheduled
# Weekly (owner, 2026-11-13). Absent also reads weekly; stated so the knob says it.
cadence weekly

# --- when -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's weekly window: Wednesday 01:00-07:00 (Tue 17:00-23:00 PST),
# set 2026-11-13. Every step's whole span must fit inside it, clear of the
# quiet ranges below, or apply.sh refuses it.
window Wed 01:00-07:00
# The first run, 2026-11-13, had a dated one-off window; it's removed now that
# it's passed (git history keeps it). The record is on #658.

# The daily audits and the prune (infra/power-map-*.timer, OnCalendar=daily,
# RandomizedDelaySec=300; each run takes 4 s or less).
quiet 00:00-00:10
# The dataset chain (docs/RUNBOOK_DESIRED_STATE.md): the pull at 09:00, the
# build and dry-run apply at 09:30, each with a 300 s delay (build ~6 s).
quiet 09:00-09:10
quiet 09:30-09:40
# The /ready (2 min), egress-IP (5 min) and anomaly (hourly) probes are
# read-only and can't be avoided. A reboot shows in co-status as
# co-power-map-ready "stopped reporting" past its 480 s grace, then "recovered".

# --- what the reboot chain stops ------------------------------------------
# Stopped before the reboot; after boot its first start is checked. That start
# runs ExecStartPre (uv sync + apply-schema.sh), which needs the managed DB.
service power-map.service

# --- the data store -------------------------------------------------------
# None local, so no datastore line and no recovery-point.sh: the database is
# DigitalOcean managed Postgres (#501), backed up by DO. The run's rollback
# path is the before-versions apply.sh records.

# --- checks (never root: they run as the invoking user, here exedev) -------
# /ready, not /health: only /ready reaches the DB, which is gated on the
# egress IP, and that can rotate across a reboot (#410,
# docs/RUNBOOK_DB_TRIAGE.md). Never restart power-map while it fails (#748).
health curl -sf -o /dev/null --max-time 10 http://127.0.0.1:8000/ready

# No inflight line: the API has no job queue, and the fixed-time jobs are
# kept clear by the quiet ranges above.

# --- third-party apt origins (maintenance lane) ---------------------------
# Followed, by site (2026-11-13). Each has 1 pending package now. Tailscale's
# postinst restarts tailscaled, which carries co-index and co-status: its
# own held step, approved on its own. Its auto-update is off on the node (set
# 2026-11-13); the tailnet default is the admin console's.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale
origin deb.nodesource.com follow
origin cli.github.com follow

# --- prunes (owner, 2026-11-13) --------------------------------------------
# Each disable ran 2026-11-13 (prune.sh, run dirs /var/backups/patching-hosts-
# prune-<name>). The review-by date is the soak: past it, prune-plan.sh names
# the next stage, and this line changes with it (references/pruning.md).
# Docker (docker.io, containerd, runc): unused since #568; exedev is still in
# the docker group until the remove or purge drops it.
exception disabled:docker 2026-12-13 unused since 568; units masked, remove after the soak
# nginx: inactive since at least 2026-09-29; nothing proxies the API.
exception disabled:nginx 2026-12-13 unused; units masked, remove after the soak
# fwupd: no firmware on a VM. The exeuntu image masks its units and deletes its
# motd conffile, so a new fwupd stops unattended-upgrade at a conffile prompt.
# Held until the purge (prune.sh --release-hold) so it can't stop the lane.
exception disabled:fwupd 2026-12-13 no firmware on a VM; image-masked, purge after the soak
exception held:fwupd 2026-12-13 conffile prompt stops the maintenance lane until the purge

# --- exceptions -----------------------------------------------------------
# The restarter scan can't follow a uv-run module. None of these starts or
# restarts a unit: they audit the DB, probe /ready or the egress IP, prune
# TTL rows, or pull and dry-run datasets, and report to co-status (infra/,
# docs/AUDITS.md). A new uv-run timer needs its line (the guard reds).
exception not-restarter:power-map-ancillary-orphans.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-anomaly.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-assignment-rel-windows.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-datasets-pull.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-desired-state.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-egress-ip.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-infra-drift.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-openapi-parity.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-prune.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-ready.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-schema-parity.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:power-map-seat-occupancy.service 2027-05-13 uv-run audit or report; starts and restarts no unit
# power-map.service's OnFailure= target logs and posts a notice; it starts
# and restarts no unit (scripts/notify_unit_failure.py).
exception not-restarter:power-map-notify-failure@.service 2027-05-13 logs and notifies on failure; starts and restarts no unit
# The journal is volatile on this image (systemd-journal-flush masked);
# reboot-chain.sh copies it last, and --post-boot reads the copy.
exception journal:volatile 2027-05-13 image masks the flush; the reboot chain copies it

# --- not declared here ----------------------------------------------------
# image-owner: left out. This repo is public and the image repo isn't, so the
# line would publish its name (gregoryfoster/skills#350).
# session:adj: left a finding on purpose. The session chain runs at -1000
# until exe.dev changes it (#586).
